      "content": "From a geopolitical standpoint, the 2011 US-led intervention in Libya is widely considered a strategic failure due to the \"liberated\" government's subsequent collapse into civil war and the rise of extremist factions in the country. While the intervention successfully achieved its initial objective of toppling the Gaddafi regime, the US and its allies failed to plan for post-conflict nation-building or secure a legitimate political transition. This uncontrolled outcome eroded the credibility of the \"R2P\" (Responsibility to Protect) doctrine and left the US with no ally in the Western Mediterranean, ultimately worsening its long-term regional stability.\n\n*(Note: I can help you outline this argument for your paper by providing specific examples of the political fallout or analyzing the strategic miscalculations the administration made.)*",
